<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korean feed millers buy 248,000T of Chinese corn.</title>
<headline>S.Korean feed millers buy 248,000T of Chinese corn.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korean feed milling companies bought a total of 248,000 tonnes of Chinese corn from Daewoo Corp last Friday through private negotiations, traders said on Monday.  </p>
<p>Traders said one buyers' group, named Big Feed Mills, bought three 30,000-tonne cargoes for delivery to the port of Inchon.</p>
<p>Big Feed Mills also bought four 12,000-tonne cargoes for delivery to the port of Kunsan.</p>
<p>The Korea Feed Association's (KFA) in Pusan bought three 30,000-tonne cargoes for delivery to the port of Ulsan and to the port of Pusan.</p>
<p>Sam Yang Co Ltd bought 20,000 tonnes for delivery by June 20 to the port of Mokpo.</p>
<p>Details of the Chinese corn purchase are as follows:</p>
<p> TONNE   BUYER   PRICE    SHIPMENT	 ETA   ARRIVAL PORT</p>
<p> 30,000  BFM     $141.55  Jul 21-Aug 10  Aug 10  Inchon</p>
<p> 30,000  BFM     $141.55  Aug 11-31	Aug 31  Inchon</p>
<p> 30,000  BFM     $141.55  Aug 21-Sep 10  Sep 10  Inchon</p>
<p> 12,000  BFM     $143.30  Jul 21-Aug 10  Aug 10  Kunsan</p>
<p> 12,000  BFM     $143.30  Aug 1-20	 Aug 20  Kunsan</p>
<p> 12,000  BFM     $143.30  Aug 11-31	Aug 31  Kunsan</p>
<p> 12,000  BFM     $143.30  Aug 21-Sep 10  Sep 10  Kunsan</p>
<p> 30,000  KFA     $141.55  Aug 1-20	 Aug 20  Ulsan</p>
<p> 30,000  KFA     $141.55  Aug 1-20	 Aug 20  Pusan</p>
<p> 30,000  KFA     $141.55  Aug 11-31	Aug 31  Ulsan</p>
<p> 20,000 Sam Yang $144     Jun 1-20	 Jun 20  Mokpo</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
